horsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T00:25:18-07:00","id":1099407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058717-constructing-the-north-in-3e?p=1099397#post1099397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Er...where's Malice Bay? I can't find it on the map.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not marked on the map but existed in previous editions. Here:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://imgur.com/55uVZCO\" target=\"_blank\">Malice Bay</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T01:32:45-07:00","id":1099411,"title":"","content":"Huh, why did I never look at this thread before? There are a number of points that I have opinions on, but I think it would be a bit gauche to pull them up weeks or months after the fact.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat description of the geographic arrangement of the icewalkers makes for a similar dynamic to what the Asian steppe nomads had with China; mostly moving around and fighting over the habitable parts of their own territory, periodically launching raids into the more arable settlements, occasionally organising into big groups that conduct major raids on the scale of full warfare (although possibly still without territorial conquest)*, and with the capacity to form a major conquering army that can establish a sizable empire.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe distinction from prior Editions being living in a different part of the region, rather than just weaving through the same territory.<br /> <br /> \u200bIf they're around Mela's Fangs, it might also give more sense to the name; if during the summer they congregated more on the northern shores, and their yearly cycle involves crossing the frozen seas to head south for the winter. <br /> <br /> \u200b*Barring, of course, military expeditions to regularly break up their confederations and reduce their population (a point I warily make, lest a reference to warfare purely for the sake of killing render my post invisible).<br /> <br /> Speaking of invisible posts:<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Inspectors are accountants, so they should be boring</div> </div> </div> </div>What in blue blazes are you on about?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":